## Running

### Run every test in this module

```bash
<exact command>
# e.g. pytest tests/<path>/ -v
```

Expected: every UT-N PASS. No warnings, no stderr noise. Pristine
output is part of the contract — see `harness-kit:tdd/SKILL.md`
§ Verify GREEN.

### Run a single UT-N

```bash
<exact command, parameterized by test name>
# e.g. pytest tests/<path>/test_<name>.py::test_<case_name> -v
# or   npx vitest run -t '<case-name>' tests/<path>/<file>.test.ts
```

Use this form when iterating in the inner TDD loop — RED, then
GREEN, on one case at a time.

### Watch mode (optional)

```bash
<exact command>
# e.g. pytest-watch -- tests/<path>/
# or   npx vitest watch tests/<path>/
```

Watch mode is for the GREEN phase only. RED still requires you to
deliberately run a freshly-written test once and watch it fail.

### Coverage (optional)

```bash
<exact command>
# e.g. pytest --cov=src/<module> --cov-report=term-missing tests/<path>/
```

Coverage is a sanity check, not a goal. Don't write tests for
coverage; write tests for behaviour.

### How NOT to run

- ✗ Skip the runner cache / re-use a stale snapshot — flaky.
- ✗ Run with `--no-fail-fast` while in RED phase — defeats "watch
  it fail at the right step".
- ✗ Patch out real code paths with mocks just to make a test pass
  (see `harness-kit:tdd/testing-anti-patterns.md`).

